# Locked UI terms

Do not invent synonyms. MCP/tool names may stay `*_record` until explicitly edited.

## Objects

- **Library** — published MCP; a named set of business info. There are **many libraries**, not one global pile. Access (who can list/open) and Lookups (call names) belong to the library. Never: dataset, database, store, catalog, MCP server, vault, notebook.
- **Item** — one thing in a library (add / open / agent fetch). May contain several sections. Never: note, record, entry, document, page, card, skill.
- **Section** — typed chunk on an item. Never: block, module, widget.

## Item fields

- **Name** — not title
- **Labels** — not tags in the UI (`tags` in the API is OK until renamed)
- **Summary** — required one-liner; this is the list/search excerpt; store it first in the body

## Section types (do not add more without asking)

- **Table** — grid
- **Checklist** — ordered steps
- **Details** — label → value
- **Description** — short prose

## Actions

Add item, Open item, Add section, Publish library

## Product sentence

You keep **libraries** of items. Auth is to a library. Each item has a name, labels, a summary, and sections. Publish a library so people and agents can look its items up.
